---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="About Linespedia | Poetry Library & Poetry Lines" 
  description="Learn about Linespedia - a sanctuary for poetic souls. Discover, share, and celebrate the beauty of words through our curated poetry collection."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-24 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif font-black mb-12 text-primary">About Linespedia</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-indigo max-w-none text-primary/80">
      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Linespedia is a digital sanctuary dedicated to preserving, celebrating, and sharing the beauty of poetry. 
        We believe that poetry has the power to inspire, comfort, and transform lives. Our mission is to make 
        poetry accessible to everyone, regardless of their background or experience with verse.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Do</h2>
      <p>
        Linespedia curates an extensive collection of poetry lines and complete poems from classical poets, 
        contemporary writers, and various cultural traditions. Our platform allows users to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Explore thousands of poems organized by category, writer, and theme</li>
        <li>Discover the meaning and context behind poetic verses</li>
        <li>Share beautiful lines on social media platforms</li>
        <li>Learn about poets and their contributions to literature</li>
        <li>Engage with poetry through our interactive features</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content Guidelines</h2>
      <p>
        Our collection includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Classic Poetry:</strong> Works in the public domain from established poets throughout history</li>
        <li><strong>Contemporary Works:</strong> Modern poetry with appropriate rights and attributions</li>
        <li><strong>Cultural Collections:</strong> Poetry and lines from diverse cultural traditions</li>
        <li><strong>Educational Content:</strong> Articles, guides, and contextual information about poetry</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content Attribution & Rights</h2>
      <p>
        We are committed to properly attributing all content. Every poem and line on Linespedia includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear author attribution</li>
        <li>Original source information when applicable</li>
        <li>Copyright or license information where relevant</li>
        <li>Public domain status for classic works</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Report Content Issues</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe any content on Linespedia infringes on copyright, violates rights, or should be modified, 
        please <a href="/copyright/">contact us with a report</a>. We take content concerns seriously and respond 
        to all reports promptly.
      </p>

      <h2>Technology</h2>
      <p>
        Linespedia is built with modern, scalable technologies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Framework:</strong> Astro (static site generation)</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> Cloudflare Workers (serverless)</li>
        <li><strong>Styling:</strong> Tailwind CSS</li>
        <li><strong>AI Features:</strong> Enhanced with Puter.js for translations and insights</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
      <p>
        We commit to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accuracy:</strong> Correct attributions and accurate content information</li>
        <li><strong>Respect:</strong> Honoring poets, writers, and copyright holders</li>
        <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> Clear information about content origins and rights</li>
        <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Making poetry available in multiple languages</li>
        <li><strong>Trust:</strong> Responsive to concerns and dedicated to ethical practices</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact & Support</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about Linespedia, content concerns, or to share feedback, 
        please <a href="/contact/">visit our contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Legal Pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a></li>
        <li><a href="/copyright/">Copyright & Report Content</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-sm text-primary/60 mt-12 pt-12 border-t border-primary/10">
        Last updated: May 9, 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
